/* book Worked example: Q: Four signals bandlimited to 4 kHz are sampled at 8 kHz, coded with 8 bits and time multiplexed with one sync bit per frame. Find the frame duration, the bits per frame, Rb, the bit duration and the slot duration.
   1. Tf = 1/fs = 1/8000 s = 125 µs.
   2. Bits per frame = N n + S = 4 × 8 + 1 = 33.
   3. Rb = 33 × 8000 = 264 000 bit/s = 264 kbit/s.
   4. Tb = 125 µs/33 = 3.79 µs; an 8-bit slot lasts 8 × 3.79 = 30.3 µs.
   5. Check: 4 × 30.3 + 3.79 = 125.0 µs, one frame.
   Answer: Tf = 125 µs, 33 bits per frame, Rb = 264 kbit/s, Tb = 3.79 µs, slot 30.3 µs. */
