/* book Worked example 2: Q: Derive the line rates of T1 and E1 from their frames, and find the bit duration and the share of the line used by overhead in each.
   1. T1: 24 slots × 8 bits = 192 bits plus 1 framing bit = 193 bits per frame. Rb = 193 × 8000 = 1 544 000 bit/s = 1.544 Mbit/s.
   2. T1 bit duration = 1/1.544 × 10⁶ s = 0.648 µs; overhead = 1/193 = 0.52 % (8 kbit/s of framing).
   3. E1: 32 slots × 8 bits = 256 bits per frame. Rb = 256 × 8000 = 2 048 000 bit/s = 2.048 Mbit/s.
   4. E1 bit duration = 1/2.048 × 10⁶ s = 0.488 µs; overhead = slots 0 and 16 = 2/32 = 6.25 % (128 kbit/s).
   5. Both carry 64 kbit/s per speech channel: 24 × 64 = 1536 kbit/s and 30 × 64 = 1920 kbit/s of speech.
   Answer: T1 1.544 Mbit/s (193-bit frames, 0.648 µs bits, 0.52 % overhead); E1 2.048 Mbit/s (256-bit frames, 0.488 µs bits, 6.25 % overhead). */
