/* book Worked example: Q: The bits 1 0 1 1 0 are sent at 1 kbit/s with level V. Give the levels in each half-bit for polar NRZ, polar RZ, AMI and Manchester (1 = low-to-high), and find Tb and the first spectral null of each code. Which codes have no DC for any data?
   1. Tb = 1/Rb = 1/1000 s = 1 ms, so each half-bit lasts 0.5 ms.
   2. First nulls: polar NRZ at Rb = 1 kHz; polar RZ at 2Rb = 2 kHz; AMI at Rb = 1 kHz (the sin²(πfTb) factor); Manchester at 2Rb = 2 kHz.
   3. Average of this word: NRZ (3 − 2)V/5 = +0.2V and RZ +0.1V, so their DC follows the data. AMI sums +V − V + V = +V over five bits, but the alternation keeps any long average near zero. Manchester is 0 in every single bit.
   4. Manchester transitions: one at each bit centre (5) plus one at each boundary between equal bits (between the two 1s), 6 in all.
   Answer:  */
